CHANGELOG
---------

# Unreleased
* Thermograms from DJI drones with a FLIR Tau camera (Zenmuse XT, XTR, and
  some XT2 files) now open; they used to fail to load
* HTI / ToolTop files now open, although measurements and metadata don't load
  yet

# 2.2.0 (2026-08-13)
* Fluke thermogram support: opens is2 files, both older binary and newer
  zip-style, from cameras such as the Ti400, Ti401p, TiS75+, and Ti25
* Fluke thermograms include the visible-light photo, embedded measurements,
  capture parameters, and the camera's embedded palette when present
* FLIR thermograms now open in the render range embedded by the camera
* A more natural double-ended temperature range slider
* The info panel is available for all file formats, not just FLIR
* The info and measurements panels survive a failed load instead of
  showing stale data
* Blackbody can now open files from a file manager's "Open with" menu for
  JPEG, PNG, and TIFF files, including from within the Flatpak sandbox
* Improved keywords and categories make Blackbody easier to find

# 2.1.0 (2026-07-20)
* Added "Open folder…" (Ctrl+Shift+O) to browse a whole directory with the
  keyboard (Left/Right/Home/End). Selecting a folder goes through the file
  chooser portal, so directory navigation now works in the Flatpak sandbox
  without broad filesystem permissions
* Reduced Flatpak permissions: dropped all static --filesystem access from
  the manifests; file access is now granted per file/folder via the portal
* On-screen previous/next arrows appear when the directory has more
  thermograms to browse through
* Pressing a navigation key when only the open file is accessible shows a
  hint with a shortcut to open the folder instead
* The image can be dragged to pan when it is larger than the window

# 2.0.0 (2026-07-18)
A major release porting Blackbody to GTK4 and libadwaita, with a redesigned
interface and many new features:

* Completely redesigned user interface, dark by default, with on-screen temperature range sliders
* Overlay view (Picture-in-Picture or MSX) next to the thermal and visible spectrum views
* Embedded measurements (spots, lines, and areas) are now drawn on the render
* Temperatures can be shown in celsius, fahrenheit, or kelvin
* Information panel showing camera metadata and GPS location, with the option to open the location in a map
* Support for loading 16-bit centikelvin PNGs
* Scroll to zoom and keyboard navigation through all thermograms in a directory
* Palette choice is remembered when opening the next thermogram
* Improved export options and clearer error messages
* More supported FLIR cameras due to upgrading to flyr==0.7.0

# 1.2.0
* Temperature in the render can be investigated by hovering over pixels
* Added a thermometer showing the colors and associated temperatures
* Allowed temperature range is now -273,15 to 1.000.000 instead of -99 to 99 (all °C)
* Thermogram renders can be saved to PNGs
* Thermograms' celsius data can be exported to tiff

# 1.1.0 (2020-12-29)
A small, incremental update to Blackbody. Improvements:

* An error message is shown if opening a thermogram fails
* When opening fails, Blackbody doesn't unload any loaded thermograms anymore
* Added logo's heat waves as a nicer placeholder when no thermogram is opened yet
* Refined headerbar controls to only be sensitive when a thermogram is opened
* Three more known-to-be-compatible cameras (FLIR C2, FLIR E5 and FLIR P60)

# 1.0.0 (2020-12-28)
First release of Blackbody. The most important features are:

* Loading FLIR thermograms from many cameras
* Loading single-band TIFFs assumed to be in °C
* Rendering to many different colors palettes, including inferno and turbo
* Specifying the thermal range to render
* Zooming in and out
* Translated to multiple languages (English, Dutch, French, German)
* Available for Linux and Windows
